        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Amra Bangali\n- People: Prabhat Ranjan Sarkar\n- Concepts: Anti-Bengali rhetoric in Indian politics, Bengalis characterized as infiltrators in Northeast India\n- Roles: Philosopher, yogi, author, social revolutionary, poet, composer, linguist\n\nFacts:\n- Prabhat Ranjan Sarkar was born on 21 May 1921 and died on 21 October 1990.\n- Prabhat Ranjan Sarkar was also known by the spiritual name Shrii Shrii Ánandamúrti and as Bábá to his disciples.\n- Prabhat Ranjan Sarkar was an Indian philosopher, yogi, author, social revolutionary, poet, composer, and linguist.\n- Amra Bangali was founded by Prabhat Ranjan Sarkar.\n- Amra Bangali was sparked by reaction against anti-Bengali rhetoric in Indian politics that characterized Bengalis as infiltrators in Northeast India.",
